.TH SHEDMAN-APPLY 1 "2026-04-25" "ShedOS" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
shedman-apply \- reconcile /etc/shedos/system.toml against live state
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B shedman apply
.RB [ -c | --config
.IR PATH ]
.RB [ -y | --yes ]
.RB [ -n | --dry-run ]
.RB [ --validate ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B shedman apply
parses
.I /etc/shedos/system.toml
and reconciles every declared section against the live system.
Reconcilers in scope:
.B [systemd]
(unit enable/disable),
.B [drop-ins]
(/etc files),
.B [snapper]
(timeline + cleanup),
.B [pacman.repos]
(/etc/pacman.conf fence),
.B [services.postgresql]
(auto-init + per-user-db),
.B [network.firewall]
(ufw),
.B [security.keyring]
(pacman-key trust),
.B [fs.mounts]
(/etc/fstab fence),
.B [kernel.cmdline]
(Limine append tokens),
.B [[users]] / [[groups]]
(additive only).
.PP
Each section can be edited via either the TOML file or the
underlying tool (e.g.
.BR ufw " " allow ", "
.BR pacman-key " " --lsign-key ).
Hand-made changes via the raw tool are
.I adopted
into the TOML on the next apply. The TOML is the canonical
persisted form; raw tool calls are a convenience UI.
.PP
Install-time state (Calamares-created users, shedos-keyring's trust
chain, pre-existing fstab entries) is snapshotted to per-section
baseline files on first apply and permanently invisible to the
reconciler thereafter.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -c " " \fIPATH\fR ", " --config " " \fIPATH\fR
Read declarative state from
.I PATH
instead of
.IR /etc/shedos/system.toml .
.TP
.BR -y , " --yes"
Apply without the interactive y/N prompt.
.TP
.BR -n , " --dry-run"
Print the plan and exit. No mutations, no TOML adoption-write.
.TP
.B --validate
Parse + schema-check the TOML; exit 0 if valid, 2 on any error. No
plan built, no live access.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/shedos/system.toml
Source of truth.
.TP
.I /usr/share/shedos/system.toml.example
Fully-commented template covering every supported section.
.TP
.I /var/lib/shedos/<section>.{state,baseline}.json
Per-section state files used by the bidirectional adoption merge.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SHEDOS_APPLY_ETC_ROOT
Override
.IR /etc .
.TP
.B SHEDOS_APPLY_STATE_ROOT
Override
.IR /var/lib/shedos .
.TP
.B SHEDOS_APPLY_BOOT_ROOT
Override
.I /boot
(used by
.BR [kernel.cmdline] ).
.TP
.BR SHEDOS_APPLY_UFW ", " SHEDOS_APPLY_PACMAN_KEY ", " SHEDOS_APPLY_SYSTEMCTL ", " SHEDOS_APPLY_FSTAB_PATH
Override the corresponding tool / file path for fixture-driven
testing.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Plan applied (or empty plan).
.TP
.B 1
Apply failed and was rolled back, or user aborted at the prompt.
.TP
.B 2
Schema or environment-shape error (TOML invalid, fstab malformed,
limine.conf parser failure).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR shedman (1),
.BR shedman-doctor (1).
